>> title: Egg Rolls
>> category: Dumplings & Rolls
>> tags: pork, cabbage, chinese, deep-fry, appetiser
>> counters: Takeout Counter
>> aka: egg roll, pork egg roll, 蛋捲, 春捲, chun juan, side order of two
>> pairs-with: sweet-and-sour-sauce
>> servings: 8
>> time: 1 hr 15 min
>> slack: narrow — the filling goes in cold, because a warm one steams inside the wrapper and bursts the seam in the oil with nothing to be done

>> step: brown the pork 4 min
Stir-fry @ground pork{8%oz}(225 g) with @garlic{3%cloves}(minced) and @fresh ginger{1%Tbs}(grated) in @peanut oil{1%Tbs} in a hot #wok{} for ~stirfry{4%min}, breaking it fine.

>> step: wilt the vegetables 3 min
Toss @napa cabbage{4%cups}(300 g; shredded), @carrot{1%medium}(julienned), @bean sprouts{1%cup}(90 g), and @scallions{3}(thinly sliced) into @&(~1)pork{} over high heat for ~stirfry{3%min}, until the cabbage collapses.

>> step: season, spread thin, cool 30 min
Season @&(~1)filling{} with @light soy sauce{1%Tbs}, @oyster sauce{1%Tbs}, @toasted sesame oil{1%tsp}, and @white pepper{1/4%tsp}, then spread it on a tray and ~cool{30%min} — a warm filling steams the wrapper from inside and the roll splits in the oil.

>> step: roll tight, seal the corner
Roll @&(~1)filling{} up in @egg roll wrappers{8}(7-in), a scant 1/3 cup each, folding the sides in and sealing the last corner with @cornstarch{1%Tbs}(slaked in 2 Tbs cold water).

>> step: fry 350°F (175°C) 5 min, drain
Fry @&(~1)rolls{} four at a time in @peanut oil{4%cups}(950 mL; at 350°F/175°C) for ~fry{5%min}, turning once, until blistered and deep gold, then drain on a rack.
